BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ambunu Plant-based Hair Care - Wellness Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T193000
UID:6a4c09489302a0b2287adf91@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of Emancipation Month\, join us to explore Ambu
 nu\, a traditional African botanical used for gentle hair cleansing and co
 nditioning. This interactive workshop highlights the rich history of herba
 l hair care practices and the benefits of plant-based ingredients for scal
 p and hair wellness.\nParticipants will learn about the science of natural
  hair care\, including how different oils support scalp health and hydrati
 on. The session features a guided\, hands-on activity where you’ll perso
 nalize a prepared Ambunu treatment using essential oils\, while also learn
 ing about the full herbal preparation and formulation process. Registratio
 n required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c09489302a0b2287adf91
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
