BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
UID:6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b5d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 17\, 2026\, 10 am-12 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery S
 aturday\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 24 - December 12\, 2026\, 10
  am-1 pm\n. Registration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto t
 ickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all par
 ticipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis progr
 am is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. G
 erstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \nperson
 al information collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b5d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
