BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Seungjoo Seo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T235959
UID:6a3d6c6c7e16a03d00e807f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Seungjoo Seo ar
 e on display at Northern District Library branch in an exhibit.\nSeungjoo 
 Seo is a Toronto-based artist and 2025 graduate of Humber Polytechnic's Vi
 sual and Digital Arts program. Working across acrylic\, oil\, and mixed me
 dia\, her art explores themes of culture\, history\, individuality\, and h
 uman challenges. She exhibited at The Lost Library in Mississauga and Deca
 gram at L Space Gallery in 2025.\n"As a Korean artist\, I explore themes o
 f healing\, identity\, and personal growth. My inspiration comes from ever
 yday life and dreams—both the ones I experience in sleep and the ones I 
 strive to achieve. Through different forms of art\, I try to express parts
  of myself and show how struggles can turn into strength. My hope is to cr
 eate work that feels open and welcoming\, giving comfort and connection to
  people who may be uncertain about their future."\nThis exhibit is part of
  TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space
  for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. The
 se exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and 
 its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Northern District Li
 brary open hours. Please check the\nNorthern District\npage before you vi
 sit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Seungjoo Seo\; "Rest in Peace"
 \; acrylic
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor art gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d6c6c7e16a03d00e807f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T180000
UID:69c30ab6b48451fc3c0b0934@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities including 
 crafts\, games\, walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\, build connect
 ions\, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in th
 e neighbourhood!\nJoin Therapy Dog Pierre who visits Parliament alternate
  Mondays from 4:30-5:30 pm.\nRefreshments provided.\nThis program is in co
 llaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd Floor Last Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c30ab6b48451fc3c0b0934
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
