BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Swati Namjoshi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a24321846d5f64f7dce27e6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Swati Namjoshi
  are on display at Bloor Gladstone Library.\nSwati is an Indian multidisci
 plinary artist\, now based in Toronto\, making it her new home. She strong
 ly believes in the power of stories and works towards illustrating authen
 tic & mindful representations of cultures\, characters\, places\, and pers
 pectives. In her curious exploration of a gendered society\, Swati create
 s autobiographical digital illustrations in black & white\; a vulnerable e
 xpression of her experiences as an artist\, a woman\, and a mother.\nSwat
 i states: "The parallels I see across cultures and the intersectionality i
 n our identity influence my art and the way I explore and embrace diversit
 y. The human experience is far more shared than it is divisive\, and I pai
 nt to contribute to the love rather than the hate. My style exhibits emoti
 ve characters embedded in their whimsical worlds. I believe presenting vul
 nerable experiences through hopeful illustrations that toy with reality an
 d exaggeration\, could nurture a sense of belonging and community."\nThis 
 exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Libra
 ry provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations acr
 oss the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests
  of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Blo
 or/Gladstone branch's open hours. Please check the\nBloor/Gladstone branc
 h\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Swati Nam
 joshi\; Bounce\; Medium: Digital Illustration Printed on Paper
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a24321846d5f64f7dce27e6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
