BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T180000
UID:69c30ab6b48451fc3c0b0935@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities including 
 crafts\, games\, walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\, build connect
 ions\, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in th
 e neighbourhood!\nJoin Therapy Dog Pierre who visits Parliament alternate
  Mondays from 4:30-5:30 pm.\nRefreshments provided.\nThis program is in co
 llaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd Floor Last Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c30ab6b48451fc3c0b0935
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Knit and Unwind
