BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Northern District Book Club—Evenings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T200000
UID:6a5f86437b79214226aa1375@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly\, spirited discussion of a different bo
 ok on the third Wednesday of each month. We read an eclectic mix of mostly
  contemporary fiction.\nThere is also an afternoon session to discuss the 
 same book on the second Wednesday of each month at 2:00 p.m.  You are we
 lcome at either or both!\nNote:\nno August meeting\nSeptember 16\, 2026:\n
 Orbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nOctober 21\, 2026:\nMaybe You Should Talk to 
 Someone\nby Lori Gottlieb\nNovember 18\, 2026:\nStone Yard Devotional\nby 
 Charlotte Wood\nDecember 16\, 2026:\nPerfection\nby Lorenzo Patronico
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5f86437b79214226aa1375
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Junk Journaling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T193000
UID:6a4d7b9cf69a18370052bc65@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Arrange and display your personal mementos in a one-of-a kind 
 memory book! Similar to scrapbooking\, junk journaling is a way to get cre
 ative with repurposed materials and to tell your story through collaging\,
  writing\, and art.\nWhether you're creating with your own ephemera—such
  as ticket stubs\, pictures\, handwritten notes\, stickers\, and more—or
  only using the upcycled craft supplies provided\, we invite you to join i
 n this fun and eco-friendly art form. Participants are encouraged to bring
  and work on their own journal during the program\, but a few small notebo
 oks will be available on a first-come\, first-served basis.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d7b9cf69a18370052bc65
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
