DESCRIPTION:Arrange and display your personal mementos in a one-of-a kind 
 memory book! Similar to scrapbooking\, junk journaling is a way to get cre
 ative with repurposed materials and to tell your story through collaging\,
  writing\, and art.\nWhether you're creating with your own ephemera—such
  as ticket stubs\, pictures\, handwritten notes\, stickers\, and more—or
  only using the upcycled craft supplies provided\, we invite you to join i
 n this fun and eco-friendly art form. Participants are encouraged to bring
  and work on their own journal during the program\, but a few small notebo
 oks will be available on a first-come\, first-served basis.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d7b9cf69a18370052bc63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Investing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T140000
UID:6a4d62e2b96ccc750c5a1185@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to investing? Learn the basics of this important part of f
 inancial literacy\, including how to save with the goal of investing\, typ
 es of investments\, how to open an account\, types of accounts\, how to av
 oid financial frauds and scams\, and more.\nPresented by Canadian Investme
 nt Regulatory Organization (CIRO)\, a national self-regulatory organizatio
 n that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers and trading a
 ctivity on Canada’s debt and equity marketplaces.\nToronto Public Librar
 y is committed to accessibility. Please call or email us if you are Deaf o
 r have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to particip
 ate in this program. Please let us know as far in advance as possible and 
 we will do our best to meet your request. At least three weeks' notice is 
 preferred. Phone (416) 393-7099 or email\naccessibleservices@tpl.ca
LOCATION:College/Shaw\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d62e2b96ccc750c5a1185
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
