DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T190000
UID:6963eb2ac967cb4120814849@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a fun\, low stress way to try new crafts and meet 
 fellow makers? Join us for DIY Night: Craft & Socials\, a monthly adult cr
 afting program featuring a new project each month. Learn something new\, w
 ork at your own pace\, and enjoy casual conversation in a welcoming space.
  Materials are provided\, and beginners are always welcome.\nRegistration 
 is required due to limited supply. However drop in on the day of is welcom
 ed for vacant spots.\nTime: Fourth Friday of each month from 5-7\nUpcoming
  Events:\nJuly 24: Origami\nTime adjustment: This program will only run fr
 om 5-6 for this month\nOrigami is the traditional Japanese art of transfor
 ming a simple flat sheet of paper into a beautiful two- or three-dimension
 al sculpture through strategic folding.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Program Room on Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6963eb2ac967cb4120814849
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
