BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists Circle: Paper Quilling
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T160000
UID:6a612b087d824676437cd43b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner or an experienced artist\, our Artis
 ts Circle program offers a welcoming space to reduce stress\, explore new 
 art techniques\, and connect with fellow art appreciators.\nFor our August
  session\, we will explore the ancient art of paper quilling. Learn how to
  roll\, shape\, and arrange small strips of paper into an intricate and 
 colourful design. No experience is necessary and all materials will be p
 rovided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a612b087d824676437cd43b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
