BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T130000
UID:69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca85f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nThu
 rsday\, July 23\, 10:00am-12:00pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\
 ,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, July 30-September 17\, 10:00am-1:00pm\n. Regi
 stration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be p
 rovided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingre
 dient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collabo
 ration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis C
 entre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information c
 ollected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe21b61ed2c2bb2e2ca85f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Avoid Legal Problems for Older Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T153000
UID:6a5d1edbdaaaf4f51a2045d7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to be better prepared to manage future issues. Retir
 ed lawyer\, Sheldon Parker\, offers general information for older adults o
 n three key topics that may likely affect them in the future: Powers of At
 torney\, Will and Codicils\, and Real Estate Ownership Issues.\nA graduate
  of Osgoode Hall Law School\, Sheldon Parker was a founding partner of Par
 ker & Zener LLP\, a law firm specializing in Real Estate\, Commercial\, Ta
 x and Estate work. Retired from active practice in early 2016\, Sheldon no
 w lectures on politics\, fraud\, elder abuse and Estate planning throughou
 t the GTA.\nRegistration is encouraged.\nDrop-ins are welcome until capaci
 ty is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5d1edbdaaaf4f51a2045d7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee and Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T150000
UID:695d7436f21d1d99bcda1b35@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and informal discussion about 
 services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and le
 t us know what information and resources you would like to access at the l
 ibrary and in the community.\nEach month we will be joined by a different 
 community organization. Upcoming guests at Lillian H. Smith branch:\nFrida
 y\, July 31:\nUniversity Settlement\nFriday\, August 28:\nHF Care – Asia
 n Mental Health and Well-Being\nFriday\, September 25\n:\nTPL staff (Indig
 enous Initiatives) and WoodGreen\nFriday\, October 30:\nVolunteer T.O.\nFr
 iday\, November 27:\nOsteoporosis Canada\nSnacks and refreshments are prov
 ided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the progr
 am.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695d7436f21d1d99bcda1b35
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T163000
UID:69583000c719ac98c335c8c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nTHHC can be contacted at 416-285-8070.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69583000c719ac98c335c8c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
