BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Need To Talk About AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T200000
UID:6a5912f30e562e28009a4ea9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about Artificial Intelligence (AI)?\nJoin us to learn 
 about and discuss aspects of this technological innovation.\nThis workshop
  series explores AI's real impacts on jobs\, privacy\, the environment\, a
 nd our communities\, while discussing how we can shape it responsibly. Eac
 h themed 90-minute session allows for small group discussion\, practical t
 akeaways and honest conversation about AI without the hype.\nOct 7 - AI f
 or the Non-Technical\nIn this session\, we tackle the\n"Elephant in the Ro
 om"\n—addressing ethics\, hallucinations\, and the fear of replacement t
 o foster a responsible\n"AI for Good"\nmindset. We demystify the technolog
 y by viewing AI as an\n"intern with a PhD in everything"\n—a tool that m
 asters five specific superpowers\, such as personalization at scale and ra
 pid research\, while leaving the irreplaceable domain of empathy\, intuiti
 on\, and creativity to you.\nOct 14 - How Do We Shape AI?\nAI is already 
 reshaping how we work\, protect our privacy\, and participate in society
 —yet most of us never get a seat at the table in deciding how it's built
  or used. This session creates that space. Equal parts presentation and co
 nversation\,
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5912f30e562e28009a4ea9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
