BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Health Matters: Staying Healthy in a Changing Climate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T200000
UID:6a502411fb418a280099da6b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Climate change is already affecting our health in a variety of
  ways\, from extreme heat and poor air quality to more frequent extreme we
 ather events. Join us to learn how these environmental changes can affect 
 your health and discover practical steps you can take to stay safe and pro
 tect your well-being.\nThis session will explore:\nHow climate change and 
 extreme weather can impact human health\nHow to recognize poor air quality
 \, high UV ratings\, and other environmental health risks\nPractical strat
 egies to help protect yourself and reduce the risk of heat- and climate-re
 lated health complications\nResources and services available to help you s
 tay safe\, including the Heatwave Registry and options for connecting with
  primary care\nAbout the Speaker\nDr. Samantha Green is a family physician
  at St. Michael's Hospital and Inner City Health Associates in Toronto. Sh
 e is also an Assistant Professor in the Department of Family and Community
  Medicine at the University of Toronto and President of the Canadian Assoc
 iation of Physicians for the Environment.\nThis program is presented by To
 ronto Public Library in collaboration with the\nWest Toronto Ontario Healt
 h Team\n(OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social service provi
 ders working together to improve the health and well-being of communities 
 in West Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis program is part of Toronto Pub
 lic Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiative\, which offers trusted he
 alth programs and resources to help people make informed decisions about t
 heir health. Learn more by exploring the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\
 nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual event is free to join but registra
 tion is required.\nPlease register on Eventbrite\n.\nOnce registered\, you
 ’ll receive an email with details on how to join the session.\nWe can’
 t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a502411fb418a280099da6b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T130000
UID:6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2756@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Tuesdays\, join us for crafts
  (11am-1pm) a walk (11:15am-1pm) and chair yoga (11:30am-12:30pm).\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Varies by program
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2756
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Craft Club: Movie Afternoons
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T170000
UID:69b057bfb48451fc3c07e9f6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Malvern Library's Craft Club runs twice a month on Tuesdays. 
 Basic supplies provided for learners.\nFirst session\n:\nJoin us in the Di
 gital Innovation Hub to make a crafting-related goodie to take home.\nRegi
 stration required.\nRegister in-person while participating in the previous
  month's session two. Any leftover spots are available to reserve online a
 fter the program ends.\nSecond session:\nDo you knit\, crochet\, hand-sew\
 , cross-stitch\, or embroider? Or are you looking to learn? Join us to st
 itch\, chat\, and have some fun while watching a cozy film.\nDrop-in.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b057bfb48451fc3c07e9f6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: Citizenship Education Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T120000
UID:6a61473f1bbbb30f3e80e67c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When you join our Citizenship Education Circle\, you will take
  part in four sessions to learn the topics like Canadian history\, geogra
 phy and government\, as well as citizenship rights and responsibilities. 
 During the program\, you will also use and work through the “Discover C
 anada” guide\, a Government of Canada document designed to teach you wha
 t you need to know to become a citizen. This is a free workshop in Englis
 h and Mandarin.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a61473f1bbbb30f3e80e67c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
