BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2SLGBTQ+ Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T200000
UID:69446bd62c65973d001356ba@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the last Wednesday of every month for a warm and li
 vely discussion of 2SLGBTQ+ books! This year we will be reading:\nJanuary\
 n: Biography of X - Catherine Lacey\nFebruary\n: Angry Queer Somali Boy - 
 Mohamed Abdulkarim Ali\nMarch\n: Firebugs - Nino Bulling\nApril\n: Rainbow
  Black - Maggie Thrash\nMay\n: Sorrowland - Rivers Solomon\nJune\n: Stag
  Dance - Torrey Peters\nJuly\n: Peaces - Helen Oyeyemi\nAugust\n: Afterpa
 rties: Stories - Anthony Veasna So\nSeptember\n: To the Moon and Back by 
 Eliana Ramage\nOctober\n: The Loves of My Life: A Sex Memoir by Edmund Wh
 ite\nNovember\n: Loveless - Alice Oseman\nPlease note that the book list 
 is subject to change.\nDrop in. No registration required.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69446bd62c65973d001356ba
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Calm and Colour - featuring a therapy dog
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T160000
UID:6a47b839541102b7fa8a2b90@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a “We Are All Related” Indigenous themed comm
 unity colouring activity led by One Health Partners in partnership with T
 oronto Public Library. Participants will get an opportunity to color indi
 vidual prints designed by Indigenous artist Caitlin Wemigwans\, which will
  be placed on a "Tree of Belonging" celebrating the interconnectedness of 
 all life\n—\nan important part of Indigenous culture as well as One Heal
 th Partners philosophy.\nThe session also features a\ntherapy dog\nand\nha
 ndler team\nfrom One Health Partners\, providing comfort\, calm and joy.
  Participants will be invited to gently interact with the dog in small gr
 oups of up to 5 people at a time.\nRegistrants will need to check-in by 3:
 05 pm to hold their spot. Drop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a47b839541102b7fa8a2b90
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
