 r. Participants are expected to commit to the duration of the course and a
 ttend all learning circle sessions.\nPython Essentials 2\nis designed for 
 learners who are already familiar with the essentials of Python\, includin
 g programming concepts like data types\, containers\, functions\, conditio
 ns\, and loops.\nRequired: completion of the\nPython Essentials 1\ncourse\
 , or equivalent experience.\nPython Essentials 2 is the second in a 2-cour
 se series that will prepare you for the\nPCAP – Certified Associate in P
 ython Programming\ncertification exam at Pearson VUE. This intermediate-le
 vel course covers\nadvanced aspects of Python programming\n\, including mo
 dules\, packages\, exceptions\, file processing\, as well as general codin
 g techniques and object-oriented programming (OOP).\nFor more information 
 about the Python Essentials 2 learning circle\, please contact\nnetworkin
 gacademy@tpl.ca\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information 
 on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public L
 ibraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will on
 ly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Q
 uestions about how the library handles your information can be directed to
  Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stree
 t\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
