BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T130000
UID:6a429fd1ed35742f00ff275a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Tuesdays\, join us for crafts
  (11am-1pm) a walk (11:15am-1pm) and chair yoga (11:30am-12:30pm).\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Varies by program
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff275a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marketing on a Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T200000
UID:6a5668d582c03c5c17d7e6b3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You don't need money to get seen - you need a strategy. In thi
 s session we will cover organic social media\, word of mouth\, community 
 partnerships\, and how to show up consistently without burning out.\nMeet 
 the Resident:\nVivian Kaye is a serial entrepreneur and business mentor wh
 o bootstrapped KinkyCurlyYaki to seven figures without outside funding. Ov
 er 15 years\, she has mentored 300+ entrepreneurs\, recently facilitating 
 workshops for FoundHers Innovation Labs and Humber College's Entrepreneurs
 hip Program.\nFeatured in The New York Times\, Toronto Star\, and on CityT
 V's Cityline\, Vivian has partnered with brands including Shopify\, Amazon
 \, and American Express Canada. Her direct\, practical approach helps earl
 y-stage Black entrepreneurs navigate the realities of building sustainable
  businesses without traditional support systems.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Meeting Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5668d582c03c5c17d7e6b3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
