BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fact or Fiction: Identifying and Combatting Misinformation and Di
 sinformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260830T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260830T153000
UID:69dd0e3e129f127438383bb2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds of all ages who want to arm th
 emselves with the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of onlin
 e information responsibly and safely.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd0e3e129f127438383bb2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T180000
UID:69fcdb28f6bd012f0066618e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more?\nDrop in for the information session on Tue
 sday\, August 4\, 2026 at 3 pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Tuesday\,\no
 nce a week for 8 weeks\, August 11-September 29\, 2026 from 3 - 6 pm\n. Re
 gistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be
  provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ing
 redient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in colla
 boration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis
  Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information
  collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, 2nd floor at the end of the hallway.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fcdb28f6bd012f0066618e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
