DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T200000
UID:6a5668d3f213992f00c42b7d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Underpricing is the silent killer of small businesses. This se
 ssion will be about understanding the difference between what something c
 osts and what it's worth - and building the confidence to charge according
 ly.\nMeet the Resident:\nVivian Kaye is a serial entrepreneur and business
  mentor who bootstrapped KinkyCurlyYaki to seven figures without outside f
 unding. Over 15 years\, she has mentored 300+ entrepreneurs\, recently fac
 ilitating workshops for FoundHers Innovation Labs and Humber College's Ent
 repreneurship Program.\nFeatured in The New York Times\, Toronto Star\, an
 d on CityTV's Cityline\, Vivian has partnered with brands including Shopif
 y\, Amazon\, and American Express Canada. Her direct\, practical approach 
 helps early-stage Black entrepreneurs navigate the realities of building s
 ustainable businesses without traditional support systems.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Meeting Room 2
