 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 3\, 2-4 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Saturday morni
 ng\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 10 - November 28\, 2:00-4:45 pm\nR
 egistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will b
 e provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. In
 gredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in coll
 aboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisi
 s Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal informatio
 n collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4e8a137d04302f001671b4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T193000
UID:6a21befe703c3363002c4438@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Locke library and its neighbourhood is home to a variety of tr
 ees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the natural 
 world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different spec
 ies and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\nChildre
 n under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThe tour will start
  and end at Locke's program room and will be guided by the City of Toront
 o Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the r
 oute. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. 
 gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This progr
 am takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, r
 egistrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThis program is part 
 of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Tor
 onto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Locke\, Meet at Program Room\, Program is offsite.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a21befe703c3363002c4438
