BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Modern Marketing: Building Awareness Without a Big Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T200000
UID:6a2c8a9b1e67cd9cb3398f8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Many entrepreneurs assume they need a large marketing budget t
 o grow their business. The reality is that some of the most effective mark
 eting strategies cost very little and rely more on consistency\, creativit
 y\, and connection.\nJoin us for a discussion on modern marketing approach
 es including content creation\, community building\, partnerships\, referr
 als\, and creator-led marketing. Participants will explore practical ways 
 to increase visibility\, attract customers\, and build momentum without re
 lying heavily on paid advertising.\nAll sessions are interactive and parti
 cipants are encouraged to bring questions related to their own business or
  entrepreneurial goals.\nMeet the Resident\n: Melanie Cruickshank is a fou
 nder and brand-side operator with over 15 years of experience building\, l
 aunching\, and scaling beauty and personal care brands. As the founder of 
 da lish cosmetics\, she led everything from product development and retail
  strategy to e-commerce growth and national partnerships. Known for her ha
 nds-on\, no-nonsense approach\, Melanie brings a founder’s accountabilit
 y and a deep understanding of what it takes to build brands that perform i
 n market.\nThis program is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nEntrepreneu
 r in Residence\nprogram series with a focus on women entrepreneurs\, desig
 ned to support women as they explore entrepreneurship and build practical 
 small business skills. Participants will learn about key topics for starti
 ng and growing a business\, with guidance from an experienced entrepreneur
  in residence. For more information and a full list of programs\, visit\nt
 pl.ca/eir\n.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c8a9b1e67cd9cb3398f8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Reflections of Nature by Brenda Sherwood
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a4c16519aae2bdc2800805f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Brenda Sherwood
  are on display at Don Mills Branch in an exhibit titled Reflections of Na
 ture.\nBrenda Sherwood is a professional photographer represented by Getty
  Images. She has had four exhibits and her photos that were sold are in pr
 ivate collections. She is also a Filmmaker and won a Gemini for her film\,
  The Bellringer. She is a member of the Academy of Canadian Cinema and Tel
 evision. Brenda Sherwood received her Honors Bachelor of Arts in 2021. Sh
 e graduated at University of Toronto with a HBA in Digital Enterprise Mana
 gement Specialist and a minor in Art History.\n"My photography captures mo
 ments in nature\, whether its animals\, flowers\, or bees. My work can be 
 recognized by a timeless quality\, and my approach to photography has alw
 ays been spontaneous and up close. Macrophotography enables me to achieve 
 this and provides me with the ability to tell stories that provoke reflec
 tion and spark dialogue. My photography is now adapted into oil paintings 
 and silk screening\, which provide me with ways to convey the images that
  I have captured."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\npro
 gram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit t
 heir work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the 
 diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibi
 t can be viewed during Don Mills branch open hours. Please check the\nDo
 n Mills\nbranch page before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage cred
 it: Brenda Sherwood\; "Mini Roses"\; photo
LOCATION:Don Mills
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c16519aae2bdc2800805f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Android Apps for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T193000
UID:6a56d0e9f213992f00c44e17@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is for beginners who are curious about buying an An
 droid phone or tablet\, or who have acquired one and want to install apps.
  Android phones include those manufactured by Samsung\, Google\, Motorola\
 , and OnePlus.\nIn this beginner's class\, you will learn about:\n- what a
 pps are\, and the benefits of using them\n- the differences between pre-in
 stalled\, free\, and paid apps\n- how to access and use the Google Play St
 ore\n- how to evaluate\, download and use apps\nAt the end of the class\, 
 you will have a basic understanding of how to install apps on your Android
  device through the Google Play Store.\nBring your own device: if you have
  an Android device\, feel free to bring it with you and follow along with 
 the exercises.\nPrerequisites:  None\nFormat:  Lecture with hands-on exerc
 ises\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a56d0e9f213992f00c44e17
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC):  Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T200000
UID:6a5974e0f213992f00c4e0cf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC) workshops are unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect. (wcc-cec.org)\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. 
 Materials are provided.\nWorkshops are not sequential\; every workshop is 
 unique - join any session and let's write together!\nSpace is limited\n. R
 egister online\, in-branch or by calling 416-393-7680.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room (downstairs)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5974e0f213992f00c4e0cf
