BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum Art Heist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T200000
UID:6a5f84670e562e28009b58eb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:On March 18\, 1990\, two men dressed as police officers broke 
 into the Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum in Boston and stole 13 masterpiec
 es worth $500M\, including five Degas\, three Rembrandts\, and a Vermeer.\
 nThis seminar will illuminate who Isabella Stewart Gardner was\, how she a
 massed thousands of pieces of art\, who may have perpetrated the heist\, t
 he implications of art theft\, and other fascinating facts about the large
 st unsolved art heist in history.\nPresented by author and artist Jerry Le
 vy.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Hosted in the discussion room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5f84670e562e28009b58eb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
