BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: Healing\, Releasing\, and Moving Forward
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T200000
UID:6a4eb7451006a63d00210bc5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Life can bring heavy burdens—grief\, loss\, or the silent ex
 haustion of caring for others. When we experience major heartbreaks\, our 
 emotional energy can feel stuck or overwhelming. You do not have to carry 
 this weight alone. This compassionate workshop offers a safe\, gentle\, a
 nd confidential space for women to honor their feelings\, release emotiona
 l pain\, and find a sense of peace.\nWhat We Will Explore:\nThe Weight of 
 Grief: How our bodies and minds hold onto unexpressed pain and stress.\nGe
 ntle Releasing: Simple\, compassionate mindfulness and breathing exercises
  to practice "letting go.\nShared Strength: Connecting with other women in
  a supportive\, non-judgmental circle.\nThis program is offered through th
 e library settlement partnership for newcomers as such the program will b
 e offered in English and Mandarin. To register please contact Wen Chen at
  647-388-3762 or wchen@ccscan.ca
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Multipurpose Room\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4eb7451006a63d00210bc5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Club: Detective Aunty
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T163000
UID:6a4457b0a03157457d04dccc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:When her grown daughter is suspected of murder\, a charming an
 d tenacious widow digs into the case to unmask the real killer in this twi
 sty\, page-turning whodunnit—the first book in a cozy new detective seri
 es from the acclaimed author of\nAyesha at Last.\nJoin us for a chat about
  the book Detective Aunty by Uzma Jalaluddin\nThis is a registered program
 \, you can register online and pick up a copy of the book in branch.
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4457b0a03157457d04dccc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
