BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesday Night Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T194500
UID:6a58e466daaaf4f51a1ff01e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Tuesday\, August 25 at 6:30 p.m. to talk abo
 ut our book of the month\,\nThe blue castle\n\, by Lucy Maud Montgomery.\n
 Valancy lives a drab life with her overbearing mother and prying aunt. The
 n a shocking diagnosis from Dr. Trent prompts her to make a fresh start. F
 or the first time\, she does and says exactly what she feels. As she expan
 ds her limited horizons\, Valancy undergoes a transformation\, discovering
  a new world of love and happiness. One of Lucy Maud Montgomery's only nov
 els intended for an adult audience\, The Blue Castle is filled with humour
  and romance.\nYou can get a copy at the first-floor circulation desk whil
 e supplies last. If you prefer an eBook or eAudiobook\, ask library staff 
 how to access them. All are welcome!\nDrop-in\, registration not required.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a58e466daaaf4f51a1ff01e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
