BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Louis Crout
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T235959
UID:6a39699a296ea565de2df509@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout July\, works by artist Louis Crout are on display a
 t Mimico Centennial branch.\nLouis Crout holds a BFA\, Fine Art\, from the
  University of Toronto\, and has also attended the Vancouver School of Art
 \, and Malaspina Printmakers.\n"I am inspired by the everyday beauty found
  where I live. As a printmaker\, I attempt to interpret the colour\, space
  and light of these scenes in the the 2-dimensional print."\nThis exhibit 
 is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library prov
 ides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the
  city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the
  city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Mimico Cen
 tennial branch open hours. Please check the\nMimico Centennial\nbranch p
 age before you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Louis Crout\
 ; "Green Boat"\; screenprint
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Mezzanine
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a39699a296ea565de2df509
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
