DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T200000
UID:6a340eb290cc4e3a790f0ad1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the 3rd Tuesday evening of every month to discuss b
 ooks in a friendly and social atmosphere.\nAugust Book Title:\nThe Laundry
 man's Boy\nby\nEdward Y.C. Lee\nSeptember Book Title:\nBreakfast of Champi
 ons\, Or\, Goodbye Blue Monday!\nby\nKurt Vonnegut\nTo get a copy of the b
 ook\, please visit the 1st floor desk at Albert Campbell Library. New memb
 ers are always welcome.\nDrop-in or register for a reminder at 416-396-889
 0 or speak to staff at the desk.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a340eb290cc4e3a790f0ad1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bridging Minds: Asthma Myths\, Modern Treatments\, and the Future 
 of Breathing Better
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T190000
UID:6a6110b57b79214226aa6d8f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Asthma is common\, but it is often misunderstood. In this talk
 \, Dr. Andrew Kouri will explain how asthma care has changed from simply t
 reating symptoms with a rescue puffer to preventing flare-ups\, personaliz
 ing treatment\, and helping people manage their condition with better tool
 s and education. He will also address common myths about asthma\, discuss 
 what current research tells us\, and share practical resources for living 
 well with asthma.\nWhat to Expect\nAsthma basics:\nUnderstand what asthma 
 is\, why symptoms come and go and how it affects the airways\nMyth-busting
 :\nLearn the truth behind common beliefs about puffers\, steroids\, exerci
 se and other asthma misconceptions\nModern asthma care:\nExplore how treat
 ment has changed\, including action plans\, prevention of flare-ups and ne
 wer therapies\nPractical resources:\nFind out where to access reliable ast
 hma education\, inhaler videos and tools to support better day-to-day asth
 ma control\nBio:\nDr. Andrew Kouri is a respirologist and clinician scient
 ist at Women’s College Hospital and an assistant professor at the Univer
 sity of Toronto. His clinical and research work focuses on asthma\, COPD\,
  digital health\, and the use of artificial intelligence to improve respir
 atory care. Dr. Kouri studies how new tools\, including clinical decision 
 support systems and large language model-based technologies\, can help pat
 ients and clinicians make better decisions about lung health.\nAbout the S
 eries\nBridging Minds: Health & Science Conversations is a partnership bet
 ween the Toronto Public Library and Women’s College Hospital. Through mo
 nthly discussions led by experts from across different clinical areas and 
 scientific disciplines\, this series provides attendees with the opportuni
 ty to engage directly with our topics and speakers and empowers communitie
 s to navigate health and science topics confidently\, inspiring a future o
 f informed decision-making.\nLearn more:\nhttps://www.womenscollegehospita
 l.ca/bridging-minds/\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual Zoom event is
  free to join but registration is required. Once registered\, you’ll rec
 eive an email with the Zoom link.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6110b57b79214226aa6d8f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
