BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grow and Start Your Business with TSBEC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T193000
UID:6a5b84f3e9de6536001c8aea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance and grow 
 your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peopl
 e. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation w
 ill give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask q
 uestions related to your business. An advisor from TSBEC (Toronto Small Bu
 siness Enterprise Centre\, formerly Enterprise Toronto) will present an ov
 erview of information related to the business planning process\, evaluatin
 g a business idea\, financing\, marketing planning\, business structures\,
  regulatory requirements\, and more.\nDrop-ins are welcome until capacity 
 is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Scarborough Civic Centre\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5b84f3e9de6536001c8aea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: English Conversation Circle (Interacthon)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T193000
UID:6a4c157fbf8ea89c03acfff4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you new to Canada? Join us for our English Conversation Ci
 rcle\; a marathon of interactive recreational\, social and informational a
 ctivities for newcomers and community members!\nInteracthon Themes:\n-Buil
 ding a digital presence\n-Stories of you through poetry\n-Creating a visio
 n board - goal setting\n-Speed-friending\n-Game booths - ring tossing\, ho
 rseshoe\, categories\n-And more!\nWhat's in it for you:\n-Try new activiti
 es\n-Meet new people and new ideas\n-Get your voice heard\n-Connect to the
  community\n-Explore your creativity\n-Let yourself go and have fun!\nTo r
 egister\, contact Claudia at cmontoya@culturelink.ca\nIn partnership with 
 Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, CultureLink & Toronto Publ
 ic Library.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4c157fbf8ea89c03acfff4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T150000
UID:6a4bdfecc52cdc3600ef279e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nAugust 5:\nWhat A
 bout Bob?\nAugust 12:\nHunt for the Wilderpeople\nAugust 19:\nLost in Amer
 ica\nAugust 26:\nIndiana Jones and the Raiders of the Lost Ark\nSeptember
  2:\nComing to America\nSeptember 9:\nSoul (2020)\nSeptember 16:\nA League
  of Their Own\nSeptember 23:\nJulie & Julia\nSeptember 30:\nYesterday (201
 9)\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments are provid
 ed for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the progra
 m.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.
 S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4bdfecc52cdc3600ef279e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
