BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Between Emotion and Stillness by Tamiko Potts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260706T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T235959
UID:6a491afc48c98c3600a46641@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July the works of artist Tamiko Potts 
 are on display at Albion Branch in an exhibit titled Between Emotion and 
 Stillness.\nTamiko Potts (she/they) is a Toronto-based\, queer\, Japanese 
 Canadian multidisciplinary artist\, filmmaker and poet who has produced do
 cumentary television and Emmy-nominated animated series’ for the past t
 wo decades. Their work examines themes of identity\, resilience\, trauma a
 nd healing as well as their deep connection with nature. Tamiko recently 
 completed a documentary on their mother’s experience in the Japanese int
 ernment camps and is currently studying art psychotherapy at CIIAT.\n"My 
 work is inspired by acrylic pouring and sumi-e painting. By combining thes
 e two mediums\, I explore the spontaneity and emotional release of poured
  acrylics contrasted against the quiet deliberation and minimalism of trad
 itional Japanese ink painting. Through the juxtaposition of elegant Japan
 ese imagery over abstract pools of colour and motion\, I reflect on themes
  of identity and resilience. Each piece balances chaos and calm\, emotion
  and reflection\, honouring heritage while embracing change".\nThis exhibi
 t is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library pro
 vides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across th
 e city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of th
 e city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Albion br
 anch's open hours. Please check the\nAlbion branch\npage before you visit.
 \nFree. All are welcome.\nPhoto credit: Tamiko Potts\,\nIwashi (Sardines)
 :\nTides of Abundance\, Oil\, acrylic\, photography\, etc.: Acrylic\, Ja
 panese brush painting\, Large
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a491afc48c98c3600a46641
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
