BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T153000
UID:6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61ddb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet weekly\,\nin-person\,\nevery Tuesday afternoon\, Se
 ptember 15 - December 8\, 2-3:30 PM (12 sessions).\nParticipants are expec
 ted to commit to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekl
 y basis.\nLearners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digita
 l badge\ndownload a certificate of completion
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2afd9cf56bd86e00b61ddb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T164500
UID:6a4e8a137d04302f001671b6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 3\, 2-4 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Saturday morni
 ng\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 10 - November 28\, 2:00-4:45 pm\nR
 egistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will b
 e provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. In
 gredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in coll
 aboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisi
 s Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \npersonal informatio
 n collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4e8a137d04302f001671b6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
