BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T150000
UID:6a4bdfecc52cdc3600ef279b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nAugust 5:\nWhat A
 bout Bob?\nAugust 12:\nHunt for the Wilderpeople\nAugust 19:\nLost in Amer
 ica\nAugust 26:\nIndiana Jones and the Raiders of the Lost Ark\nSeptember
  2:\nComing to America\nSeptember 9:\nSoul (2020)\nSeptember 16:\nA League
  of Their Own\nSeptember 23:\nJulie & Julia\nSeptember 30:\nYesterday (201
 9)\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments are provid
 ed for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the progra
 m.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.
 S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4bdfecc52cdc3600ef279b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
