BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between the Lines Bookclub
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T200000
UID:6962837f91e4576f847bd102@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Become a page-turner by joining the Between the Lines Book Clu
 b! Here\, we embark on a new chapter with every read\, diving into a world
  of endless possibilities. From gripping thrillers to heartwarming coming-
 of-age tales\, or a sprinkle of fantasy adventures\, there's something for
  everyone. Whether you're a die-hard fan of one genre or love mixing thing
 s up\, you'll find a place here to discuss\, share\, and connect with fell
 ow readers. Ready to explore different worlds and discover your next favor
 ite book? Join us and let's turn the page together!\nFriday July 17\n: Whe
 re the Crawdad Sings by Delia Owens\nWhere the Crawdads Sing\nis a beauti
 fully written novel that blends mystery\, coming-of-age\, and romance. Set
  in the marshes of North Carolina\, it follows Kya Clark\, a young girl wh
 o grows up isolated from society and finds comfort in the natural world. A
 s the story unfolds\, themes of loneliness\, resilience\, love\, and belon
 ging intertwine with the investigation of a local man's death. It's a comp
 elling read that invites discussion about human nature\, prejudice\, and o
 ur connection to the world around us.\nIf you need help getting a copy of 
 the book or have any questions\, please contact us at sastaff@tpl.ca or 41
 6-393-7653. Copies of the monthly titles are available at the circulation 
 desk.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6962837f91e4576f847bd102
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
