BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour **NEW DATE**
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T153000
UID:6a5937e50e562e28009a56fb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Dufferin/St. Clair library and its neighbourhood is home t
 o a variety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to exp
 lore the natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recogni
 ze different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological imp
 ortance.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRe
 gistration is required.\nThe tour will start and end at the Dufferin/St. 
 Clair library ramp entrance and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urb
 an Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route.
  Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. glove
 s/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program ta
 kes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, regist
 rants will be notified of an alternative date.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Dufferin/St.Clair\, Meet at Dufferin/St. Clair library ramp entra
 nce
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5937e50e562e28009a56fb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T130000
UID:69a0e9296724c63d00f579ab@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on Sat
 urday\, June 13\, 2026\, 10 am-12 pm.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Saturd
 ay\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, June 20-August 15\, 2026\, 10 am-1 pm\n. 
 There will be no session on Saturday\, August 1. Registration closes afte
 r week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and
  refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be
  available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerste
 in Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely res
 ponsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected through th
 e program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a0e9296724c63d00f579ab
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
