BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start & Grow Your Business with TSBEC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T183000
UID:6a4f9d2164ed854800a4d585@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance and grow 
 your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peopl
 e. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation w
 ill give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask q
 uestions related to your business. An advisor from TSBEC (Toronto Small Bu
 siness Enterprise Centre\, formerly Enterprise Toronto) will present an 
 overview of information related to the business planning process\, evaluat
 ing a business idea\, financing\, marketing planning\, business structures
 \, regulatory requirements\, and more.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4f9d2164ed854800a4d585
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: WORDLY by Jacinto Salcedo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T203000
UID:6a46864648c98c3600a3e5bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, the works of artist Jacinto Sal
 cedo are on display at Leaside branch in an exhibit titled\nWORDLY\n.\nJac
 into Salcedo is a Venezuelan-Canadian award-winning graphic designer whose
  practice is rooted in simplicity\, resourcefulness\, and emotional impac
 t. For him\, design is more than aesthetics—it is strategy\, vision\, an
 d problem-solving. Salcedo brings discipline\, curiosity\, and a critical 
 eye to his work. With a passion for creating meaningful visual experience
 s\, he seeks to deliver creative solutions that bridge function and artist
 ry\, always guided by the conviction that design can make people.\n"WORDL
 Y is a series of paintings that explores the power of visual representatio
 n of words. Each work is both text and image\, drawing attention to how l
 anguage shifts meaning when it transcends the page and enters the realm of
  visual art. By painting words\, Salcedo pretends to disrupt their familia
 rity\, asking viewers to not only read but to see language\, to feel its w
 eight\, texture\, and presence. In a world where computer-generated text a
 nd templates are the norm. Salcedo explores the simplicity."\nThis exhibi
 t is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides 
 space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city
 . These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city
  and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Leaside Branch 
 open hours. Please check the\nLeaside Branch\npage before your visit.\nFre
 e. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Jacinto Salcedo\; Title of Piec
 e: HURT\; Medium: Acrylic
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a46864648c98c3600a3e5bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260814T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260814T130000
UID:69e92c5bbd9a3c316a54b254@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Fridays\, join us for crafts 
 (11am - 1pm)\, exercise (11:30am - 12:30pm)\, and Ozzy the therapy dog (al
 ternate Fridays).\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participan
 ts. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is i
 n collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e92c5bbd9a3c316a54b254
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
