BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T190000
UID:6a1776422ea730c17ab23c61@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by the\nToronto Em
 ergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in partnership with
  the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:\nThe potential
  hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to 
 assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networks d
 uring emergencies\nFree program. Register for a reminder. For more informa
 tion\, please contact the branch.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1776422ea730c17ab23c61
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Documentary Screening: Nechako: It Will Be a Big River Again
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T200000
UID:6a639de0cca66c2f00a5b8f1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Nechako\nis a crucial documentary that follows two Indigenous 
 Nations fighting for our collective future. When the Kenney Dam was built 
 in the 1950s\, the Nechako River was forever changed. The Stellat’en and
  Saik’uz Nations embarked on a groundbreaking legal proceeding against t
 he Canadian government and Rio Tinto Alcan that lasted over a decade—a b
 attle that continues today. Following community members living day to day 
 on the river while they take on powerful institutions\,\nNechako\nis an ur
 gent call to action to restore a river and a way of life.\n2025. 90 minute
 s.\nThis screening is presented in collaboration with the National Film B
 oard of Canada\, which is Canada’s only public producer and distributo
 r of Canadian films and series.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a639de0cca66c2f00a5b8f1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T150000
UID:6a18abbc46d5f64f7dcd369f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nJune 3:\nE.T. The
  Extra-Terrestrial\nJune 10:\nMadagascar 2\nJune 17:\nAbout a Boy\nJune 24
 :\nIndiana Jones and the Raiders of the Lost Ark\nJuly 8:\nAlmost Famous\
 nJuly 15: Starman (1984)\nJuly 22:\nA Star is Born\n(2018)\nJuly 29:\nBrid
 get Jones Diary\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshmen
 ts are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available 
 at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Ce
 ntre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a18abbc46d5f64f7dcd369f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Business Inc Newcomer Series - Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T200000
UID:6a36efb216554cd59fca2524@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our Fall 2026 Business Inc. Info Session to learn about t
 his 8-week program supporting Toronto entrepreneurs to launch and grow.\nD
 o you have a small business or idea and want tailored feedback and support
  to take it to the next level? Join the Business Inc. Program to connect w
 ith experienced mentors and other entrepreneurs that will help you grow.\n
 During eight weekly sessions\, entrepreneurs will learn business fundament
 als\, get clarity on the viability of their business ideas\, get feedback 
 and reviews from professional business advisors\, discuss with and learn f
 rom their peers\, and build a foundation for success.\nThe program will ru
 n weekly at Runnymede on Wednesday evenings from October 7 – November 25
 \, from 6 - 9pm.\nJoin us at our Information Session to learn more about t
 his program\, meet the instructor\, and ask any questions you may have abo
 ut your application.\nLearn about\nBusiness Inc.\n\, an eight-week busines
 s program offered in partnership with the Toronto Business Development Cen
 tre.\nRegistration is required. To register\, click\nhere\n.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a36efb216554cd59fca2524
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google AI Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T160000
UID:6a17599543b41b3d00699e6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about artificial intelligence or want to learn practic
 al AI skills for work and personal use? Join our staff-facilitated learnin
 g circle to complete the self-paced Google AI Essentials specialization.\n
 This 10-hour introductory-level specialization\, offered through Coursera\
 , is available for free to learning circle participants. It is made up of 
 five courses\, each containing four units that consist of short videos\, a
 rticles\, assignments and a short multiple-choice quiz.\nBy completing the
  specialization\,\nyou will learn:\nHow AI works\nHow to write effective p
 rompts\nHow to use generative AI tools responsibly\nHow to identify AI's p
 otential biases and avoid harm\nHow to stay up to date with AI news\nAfter
  you complete the course\, you earn a Google certificate and a badge to sh
 are with others\nLearning Circles are study groups guided by\nlibrary staf
 f for people who want to complete the Google AI Essentials specialization 
 together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work together thr
 ough course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit to attending a
 ll four learning circle sessions.\nNo AI experience is required.\nHow to J
 oi\nn a Learning Circle:\nRegister once on the first session of this event
  series\, in order to attend all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a\nvalid e
 mail address\n.\nA valid TPL library card is required for online circles
 .\nAttend all four sessions online via Zoom\, July 9\, 16\, 23\, and 30 fr
