BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Elaine Logashov
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a381bd7f56bd86e00b825c5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, the works of artist Elaine Loga
 shov are on display at Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre.\nElaine lo
 ves exploring the gritty\, urban parts of the city - alleyways\, neglected
  corners\, and places where signs of human life linger in grime. What sta
 rted as a hobby has grown into a passion\, with more time dedicated to cre
 ating art. Inspired by urban decay and overlooked spaces\, the work captu
 res beauty and emotion in the worn-down and forgotten.\n"I see beauty in t
 he overlooked and worn parts of the city - alleys\, grime\, and signs of h
 uman life. My work captures the grit and decay of urban spaces\, especial
 ly in Toronto\, which has both gritty\, hidden corners and polished\, upsc
 ale areas. I leave my pieces purposely unfinished to reflect how these gr
 itty places are often second thought and unnoticed. Art is my way of seein
 g the beauty in the neglected and the overlooked\, and sharing that persp
 ective with others.\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. 
 Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their w
 ork at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the divers
 e cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can 
 be viewed during Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre open hours. Plea
 se check the\nOakwood Village Library and Arts Centre\nbranch page before
  you visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Elaine Logashov\, "Unt
 itled"\, acrylic on canvas
LOCATION:Oakwood Village Library and Arts Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a381bd7f56bd86e00b825c5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
