BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Alone in Density by Young Hee Sung
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T235959
UID:6a3acf1b3efcc843503590a1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, the works of artist Young Hee 
 Sung are on display at North York Central Library in an exhibit titled Alo
 ne in Density.\nYoung Hee Sung is a multidisciplinary artist and the foun
 der of Laird Art Gallery in Toronto. Her practice blends Korean brush pain
 ting and Western abstraction to explore impermanence\, memory\, and transf
 ormation. She has held solo exhibitions at Assembly Hall Gallery\, Laird A
 rt Gallery\, and Ajax City Hall\, and exhibited internationally in Los Ang
 eles\, New Jersey\, and Seoul. She also curates collaborative projects tha
 t merge visual art with literature and community engagement.\n"Young Hee S
 ung is the founder of Brush Densityism\, a method of layering countless br
 ushstrokes\, dots\, and lines to create dense fields of rhythm\, energy\, 
 and colour. Rooted in the intuitive vitality of Korean brush painting and 
 the structured language of Western abstraction\, her work explores imperma
 nence\, memory\, and transformation. Expanding into sculpture and text\, s
 he creates participatory experiences where painting\, poetry\, and communi
 ty converge in renewal."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits Spac
 e\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exh
 ibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflec
 t the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe 
 exhibit can be viewed during North York Central Library open hours. Pleas
 e check the\nNorth York Central Library\npage before you visit.\nFree. All
  are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Young Hee Sung\; "Uphill"\; acrylic o
 n canvas
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd floor Gallery space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3acf1b3efcc843503590a1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
